From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:06:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input, dialogs, AudioEngine: add what a hosted client needs

A Wayland client hosted by Kodi takes keyboard and touch input, may use
Kodi's on-screen keyboard and may hand Kodi encoded audio. Let a
keyboard event handler take events before Kodi translates them into
actions, and a touch event handler take raw touch points before Kodi
recognises gestures in them, tell whether a keyboard with letter keys is
attached on GBM and how large the screen is, as its touch screen
measures it or else as its EDID tells, tell whether the user's language
is written right to left, let a keyboard dialog derived from the generic
one choose its own window, and unpack the frame of an IEC 61937 burst.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
